# Cloudflare Pages headers for the node page. Copied verbatim into dist/ by Vite (it is a public/ file).
#
# The only thing that actually needs saying here is cache lifetime. Vite hashes everything under /assets/, so
# those are immutable; the rest ships at fixed paths and changes contents whenever the aigg-porw submodule moves.
# A browser holding a cached /porw/ module against a freshly deployed bundle computes a model_id that no longer
# matches the registry -- a silently rejected claim, not an error anyone would see. Five minutes of freshness
# costs a conditional request and removes that failure entirely.
#
# Deliberately absent: COOP/COEP. The node runs the single-memory kernel in a plain worker and never touches
# SharedArrayBuffer, and require-corp would force every cross-origin fetch -- including a 28 MB brain from the
# mirror or a Greenfield SP -- to be CORS-clean or carry CORP. Also absent: a connect-src CSP, because the
# relayer URL and the brain URL are both typed in by whoever is running the node.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/porw/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/node_worker.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
